                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is a mockery of its \"source\" material. The controls are terrible even if I could have remapped the buttons or the joystick axis, which wasn't even an option. The tank is the best thing about the art and that's not saying much. I don't know why this was done in a custom engine instead of literally anything else available. The physics are atrocious, with hitboxes that do not even remotely agree with the graphics, and I finally gave up when I fell through the world and never hit a kill plane despite waiting for over five minutes.\n\nThe level design is beyond bad and is something I would have done better at than when I was doodling on paper back in grade school. Blind death jumps everywhere with no indication of what you're about to get into, and the 3d platforming is a cruel joke, only made immeasurably worse by the abysmal camera angles that this game inflicts upon you.\n\nThe music is the best part of the game in that it's merely acceptable rather than torturous trash.\n\nThis is the first game I've purchased on Steam that made me want a refund. At least when I was gifted Bad Rats I knew exactly what I was getting into accepting it.\n\nNow I feel sorry for my two brothers, whom I gifted copies of this game on the hopes that it would be at least enjoyable.\n\nI think I would rather play Blaster Master 2 for a full weekend on loop than ever sully my monitor with this \"game's\" presence again.",
